# Phase 006 — health and metric semantics

Status: **Phase 006 is ACTIVE. Groups 01–04 are accepted with HLTH-001–HLTH-040. Group 05 — Transformation Reconciliation & Metric Propagation is next and has not started.**

Phase 006 uses `HLTH-###` refinement identifiers. They refine existing concepts and do not extend SYN/REF/AUTH ranges or create hidden truth owners.

Accepted delivery order:

1. Measurement Vocabulary, Metric Families, Profiles & Applicability — **accepted**.
2. Structural / Schema / DDL Compatibility — **accepted**.
3. Baselines, Comparability, Distribution & Statistical Context — **accepted**.
4. Expectations, Thresholds, Margins, Waivers & Assessment Semantics — **accepted**.
5. Transformation Reconciliation & Metric Propagation — **next**.
6. Composite Health, Readiness Suitability & Progressive Result Timing — planned.
7. Consolidation / Exit Review — planned.

## Group 01 accepted rules — HLTH-001–HLTH-008

- metric definition ≠ metric Observation ≠ Assessment;
- calculation/extraction success ≠ health pass;
- every material measurement binds exact subject + definition/version + grain/population + window + relevant output/data/schema/current-cycle context + material time context;
- same display name ≠ same definition/version;
- formula/denominator/filter/unit/grain/window/missing-value/approximation changes require explicit version handling;
- canonical families: operational/output; temporal/freshness; structural/schema; volume/population; completeness/missingness; uniqueness/key integrity; validity/domain; distribution/shape; relational/transformation integrity; business-semantic;
- applicability ≠ profile selection ≠ technical support ≠ current availability ≠ Assessment outcome;
- available statistic ≠ useful routine metric;
- profile roles are core operational/table, critical-field/business, transformation-specific reconciliation, diagnostic/on-demand;
- diagnostic use does not automatically create permanent monitoring;
- metric/check Observations retain definition/source/scope/time/coverage/approximation/restriction provenance;
- local metric existence does not imply downstream propagation.

## Group 02 accepted rules — HLTH-009–HLTH-018

Preserve:

**declared/governed schema meaning ≠ normative structural Expectation/contract ≠ proposed/planned structural state ≠ realized structural Observation/Change ≠ compatibility Assessment**.

- bind compatibility to consumer-visible interface/contract, not merely producer physical table;
- add/drop/rename/reorder/type/precision/nullability/default/generated/key/grain/nested changes remain independently representable;
- rename identity requires evidence; drop/add coincidence is insufficient;
- same name does not guarantee same semantic identity;
- additive/removal/type/order compatibility is consumer-specific;
- engine cast/parse capability ≠ structural compatibility;
- current zero-null data does not preserve a non-null structural guarantee;
- key/grain changes can invalidate volume/uniqueness/distribution/join assumptions without automatically being defects;
- compatibility is consumer/interface/version scoped and non-transitive;
- pre-deployment/prospective validation ≠ realized production validation;
- structural change triggers scoped metric/profile/Baseline review, not global reset;
- `compatible` requires positive applicable evidence and sufficient contract coverage;
- structural incompatibility ≠ execution failure ≠ exposure ≠ Impact ≠ causality;
- do not choose validation placement during Phase 006.

## Group 03 accepted rules — HLTH-019–HLTH-029

Preserve:

**Observation ≠ reference-set membership ≠ Baseline summary/version ≠ comparative Assessment ≠ normative Expectation/health**.

- Baseline reference membership binds subject, metric definition/version, grain/population, structural/interface regime, context, window, calendar/cohort, evidence coverage and inclusion/exclusion semantics.
- Available history is not automatically eligible reference history.
- Comparability is multidimensional and conclusion-relative; do not create a universal numeric comparability score.
- Bounded states include directly comparable, comparable under explicit normalization, non-comparable, insufficient reference, ambiguous, conflicting, unavailable, unknown/unresolved and not applicable.
- Fixed/reference-period, rolling/adaptive, seasonal/cadence, cohort and post-change/new-regime Baselines are functional classes, not algorithms.
- Recency does not override business-calendar/cadence/cohort context.
- Realized metric/grain/population/key/denominator/semantic/interface/method changes can segment affected reference regimes only; unaffected dimensions can retain continuity.
- Change Intent predicts a break but does not activate it; post-change Baselines derive from realized evidence, never planned targets.
- Reference sufficiency is conclusion-relative; no universal sample minimum exists.
- Low-volume/denominator size, temporal coverage, missing periods, cohort coverage and operating variability constrain comparative strength.
- Approximate/sampled metrics can be valid evidence when method identity/limitations remain explicit.
- Differences within material measurement uncertainty must not be presented with false precision.
- Distribution references remain purpose-driven; quantiles require semantically ordered dimensions; no universal drift score.
- Raw values can be non-comparable while an explicit versioned normalized metric remains comparable.
- Normalization does not rewrite raw comparability or repair unrelated semantic breaks.
- Rolling/adaptive Baselines require explicit window progression, lag/holdout, exclusion and version semantics.
- Current Observation must not silently redefine the reference used to assess itself.
- `Looks anomalous` alone cannot justify excluding history; exclusions require independent provenance-bearing basis.
- Repeated abnormal behavior can become descriptively typical without becoming normatively acceptable.
- Multiple plausible Baselines do not receive newest/largest/narrowest/broadest/closest hidden precedence.
- Historical Baseline versions and Assessments remain preserved across refresh/regime replacement.

## Group 04 accepted rules — HLTH-030–HLTH-040

Preserve:

**Expectation/criterion ≠ Observation evidence ≠ Baseline comparison ≠ normative Assessment outcome ≠ warning/proximity ≠ severity/priority ≠ waiver/response disposition ≠ composite health**.

- criteria bind subject/dimension, metric/check/structural definition, grain/population/window/context, operator/direction, inclusive/exclusive boundary, unit/denominator and required reference basis;
- display/vendor shorthand does not invent comparison semantics;
- warning/proximity can coexist with `meets` and is not a substitute for `violates` or severity;
- relative criteria explicitly bind the reference and formula; Baseline remains descriptive generally;
- if a required reference is non-comparable/ambiguous/insufficient/unavailable, that relative normative evaluation can become indeterminate;
- authoritative criterion + unsuitable evidence does not create pass/fail;
- approximate evidence can support a result only when material uncertainty cannot change the boundary side or an explicit valid treatment applies;
- preserve `meets`, `violates`, `indeterminate/insufficient evidence`, `conflicting`, `unavailable`, and `not applicable` for a bound criterion;
- Baseline typicality and normative outcome coexist independently;
- a new regime can lack a Baseline while an independent explicit Expectation remains evaluable;
- distinct context/dimension rules can coexist; same-proposition incompatible rules remain conflict absent explicit resolution/composition;
- no strictest/loosest/newest/business/technical/highest-severity hidden precedence;
- `violates + waived response` differs from a bounded exception that makes a criterion non-applicable;
- waiver does not mutate evidence or automatically propagate across alert/gate/control consequence classes;
- severity/priority does not decide criterion outcome; Criticality does not automatically tighten thresholds or prove Impact;
- missing telemetry does not prove violation absent sufficient opportunity/coverage;
- historical criterion/reference/waiver versions remain bound to historical Assessment;
- corrected evidence creates reassessment rather than silent historical mutation.

## Group 05 boundary

Next define transformation-aware reconciliation over the accepted local measurement/reference/normative semantics.

Preserve:

- Lineage relation ≠ metric propagation ≠ status propagation ≠ causality;
- local upstream metric/Observation ≠ downstream-relevant context ≠ derived reconciliation measurement;
- local `warning`, `violates`, severity, waiver or Baseline atypicality does not propagate automatically to downstream assets;
- A+B→C never implies generic row-count arithmetic;
- join/filter/aggregation/dedupe/union semantics determine valid relationships;
- current-cycle/freshness alignment and grain/key compatibility matter to reconciliation;
- uncertainty, non-comparability, unavailability and restriction limitations remain attached to derived evidence;
- multiple abnormal upstream contributors can remain relevant without becoming causal attribution;
- Group 05 may create reconciliation Observations/Assessments through existing concepts, not a hidden propagation truth owner;
- do not define overall/composite health until Group 06.

## Permanent phase boundaries

- Do not weaken REF-001–REF-030 evidence standards.
- Do not reopen AUTH-001–AUTH-053 authority/authorization/disclosure decisions merely to simplify health semantics.
- Authority cannot manufacture empirical comparability or evidence sufficiency.
- Waiver does not rewrite Observation/Assessment or create false pass.
- Do not silently absorb incidents into adaptive Baselines or exclude history merely because it appears anomalous.
- Do not use planned/target values as empirical Baseline evidence.
- Do not hide sampling/approximation/low-volume limitations behind false precision.
- Do not collapse warning, violation, severity and waiver into one status.
- Do not invent hidden threshold tolerance/boundary semantics.
- Lineage does not recursively propagate metrics or statuses.
- Upstream anomaly/violation does not automatically become downstream failure or cause.
- High-consequence eligibility does not make stale/unavailable/immature evidence usable.
- Passive monitoring remains out-of-band/non-blocking for ungated production.
- Do not select Metric Views/DQX, GitHub Actions, Unity Catalog, anomaly/statistical algorithms, storage, streaming, caching, scheduler/orchestrator or service topology during Phase 006.

Do not begin Group 05 or a later group without explicit user direction.
